<script>
  import reports from '#lib/data/reports-4471.json';
  import notes from '#lib/data/desk-notes.json';
  import { groupByCause, readAs, uniqueById } from '#lib/kb/causes';
  import { tenantOf } from '#lib/kb/locales';
  import CauseTable from '#lib/kb/CauseTable.svelte';
  import Callout from '#lib/kb/Callout.svelte';
  import RenderStamp from '#lib/kb/RenderStamp.svelte';

  const TICKET = 4471;
  const rows = reports.length;
  const merged = uniqueById(reports).filter((r) => r.mergedInto === TICKET);
  // The desk's own view: every report filed under its cause by tenant and form, the desk's
  // one-day notes counted where they are filed (causes.ts, readAs).
  const groups = groupByCause(merged, tenantOf);
  const oneDay = groups.reduce((n, g) => n + readAs(g, notes.oneDayMove), 0);
  const count = (cause) => groups.find((g) => g.cause === cause)?.reports.length ?? 0;
  const tenantsOf = (cause) => groups.find((g) => g.cause === cause)?.tenants ?? 0;
  const parser = count('parser');
  const hint = count('hint');
  const parserTenants = tenantsOf('parser');
  const hintTenants = tenantsOf('hint');
  const unplaced = count('unplaced');
  const subjects = new Set(merged.map((r) => r.subject)).size;
  const tagHint = merged.filter((r) => r.meta.intakeTag === 'hint').length;
</script>

[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says the {merged.length} date reports are one bug: the parser reads
dates month first. The reports describe **three** problems. The fix queued for #4471 fixes the
first one only.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Three problems, three tickets. Keep #4471 open for the parser and track the other
two on their own tickets.
</Callout>

## The three problems

| problem | what the reporter sees | reports | fixed by the #4471 fix |
|---|---|---|---|
| [1 · parser reads day-first dates month first](https://github.com/ttnsy/what-it-shows/issues/1) | day and month swapped: 7 April arrives as 4 July | **{parser}** from {parserTenants} tenants | yes |
| [2 · booking-v3 form hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`](https://github.com/ttnsy/what-it-shows/issues/2) | day and month swapped, on bookings typed into the booking-v3 form | **{hint}** from {hintTenants} tenants | no |
| [3 · date moves by one day](https://github.com/ttnsy/what-it-shows/issues/3) | the right month, one day early or late: Tuesday becomes Monday | **{oneDay}**, counted inside problem 1 | no |

{#if unplaced}<p>{unplaced} reports come from tenants that are not on file. They have no cause yet.</p>{/if}

### 1 · The parser

Ticket: [ttnsy/what-it-shows#1](https://github.com/ttnsy/what-it-shows/issues/1)

The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on #4471 writes the day first, so a
date with a day of 12 or less comes out with day and month swapped. This is what #4471 describes,
and the queued fix is for this problem.

### 2 · The booking-v3 hint

Ticket: [ttnsy/what-it-shows#2](https://github.com/ttnsy/what-it-shows/issues/2)

Tenants on `booking-v3` print `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their people type what the hint
says, month first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The result looks the
same as problem 1, but the parser is not involved: the date is already wrong when the form reads
it. The parser fix does not touch it. The fix is the hint, or the form's read order.

Intake tagged {tagHint} reports as `hint`. Intake guesses from the reporter's browser, not from
the tenant and the form, so that tag does not count this problem. The count above comes from
the tenant's form and the channel the report came in by.

### 3 · The one-day move

Ticket: [ttnsy/what-it-shows#3](https://github.com/ttnsy/what-it-shows/issues/3)

These reports do not describe a swap. The date keeps its month and moves one day: "Tuesday 6
October showed as Monday", and one meeting showed as Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto.
That is a time-zone or offset problem in how a date becomes an invite. The desk already noted
these reports (desk notes, `oneDayMove`). The desk files them under the parser by tenant, so the
{parser} parser reports include these {oneDay}. They need their own ticket, because a parser fix
will not change them.

## How the count was made

- The ticket export has {rows} rows, and some reports appear twice because the export's pages
  overlap. One id is one report: {merged.length} reports.
- The cause comes from the tenant and the form, as in `causes.ts`, not from the subject or from
  intake's tag. All {merged.length} reports came in under {subjects} different subjects. A subject is not
  a cause.
- The counts are the desk's own view, as exported: the table below. The one-day reports stay
  where the desk files them, under the parser, and are counted again on their own ticket.

